    "0001193125-26-337928": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "Q2 2026 Shareholder Letter Over the first half of 2026, we’ve delivered some of our strongest results in years. In Q2, that momentum accelerated as we exceeded our outlook across every key metric.",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
    },
    "0001193125-22-274904": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "Q3 2022 Nights and Experiences Booked 99.7M In Q3 2022, Nights and Experiences Booked grew 25% compared to the prior year, driven by strength in all regions. 25% Y/Y Gross Booking Value (GBV) $15.6B Strong growth in Nights and Experiences Booked combined with continued higher Average Daily Rates (“ADR”) drove nearly 31% Y/Y $16 billion of GBV in Q3 2022. 40%",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
    },
    "0001193125-24-194849": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "Q2 revenue of $2.75 billion increased 11% compared to Q2 2023 primarily driven by the growth of nights stayed on the platform. We generated $555 million of net income during Q2 2024 and delivered a 20% net income margin, demonstrating significant profitability.",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
    },
    "0001193125-25-026054": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "Key Financial Measures Q4 2024 FY 2024 Revenue $2.5B $11.1B Q4 revenue of $2.5 billion increased 12% compared to Q4 2023 primarily driven by the growth of nights 12% Y/Y 12% Y/Y stayed on the platform. 12% Y/Y (ex-FX) 12% Y/Y (ex-FX) Net Income $461M $2.6B We generated $461 million of net income during Q4 2024 and delivered a 19% net income margin. 19% Net i",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
    },
    "0001193125-23-139392": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "In Q1, Nights and Experiences Booked hit a record high with over 120 million. Revenue of $1.8 billion grew 20% year-over-year (24% ex-FX).",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
    },
    "0001193125-23-039008": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "Revenue of $1.9 billion increased 24% from Q4 2021 demonstrating continued strong travel demand. Our first full GAAP profitable year (23% net margin) included our most profitable Q4 ever (17% net margin)—both periods delivering double digit year- over-year margin expansion.",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
    },
    "0001193125-21-056952": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "• Despite the pandemic in 2020, Airbnb’s business proved highly resilient, with strength in North America, domestic travel, nearby travel, and long-term stays. • Airbnb attracted nearly $24B of bookings in 2020 based on the inherent adaptability of the platform to support a wide range of use cases.",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
    },
    "0001193125-21-320113": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "Airbnb saw continued strength in Nights and Experiences Booked in both North America and EMEA and acceleration in Latin America, all of which have driven significant year-over- year growth. Strong recovery in Nights and Experiences Booked combined with significantly higher Average Daily Rates (“ADR”) drove nearly $12B of bookings in Q3 2021.",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
    },
    "0001193125-26-449727": {
      "h": "",
      "q": "Q3 2026 Upstate NY cabin with views of fall foliage And we’re continuing to accelerate the pace of innovation.",
      "t": [
        "earnings"
      ]
